<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Dell downgraded.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Dell downgraded.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Bear Stearns lowered its recommendation on Dell Computer Corp to attractive from buy, according to the office of analyst Andy Neff.</p>
<p>-- His office confirmed an earlier item attributed to market sources.</p>
<p>-- The downgrade was made because of the stock's current price, &quot;which is at the high end of the historic valuation range,&quot; his office said.</p>
<p>-- The fundamental view of the company is unchanged, according to Neff's office, as are the earnings estimates: $4.40 per share in 1997 and $5.50 per share in 1998.</p>
<p>-- In midmorning Nasdaq trade, the shares were off 1-5/16 to 83-5/8.</p>
<p>-- The year-high is 87-1/2 and the year-low is 23.</p>
</text>
